{{Cannabis in Balisca}}{{Life in Balisca}}
'''Cannabis in Balisca''' is fully legal for both [[w:cannabis (drug)|recreational]] and [[w:Medical cannabis|medicinal]] purposes. It is widely used, considered now almost as part of Baliscan culture. It is quite common to see people smoking or rolling in the streets and parks, and growshops in nearly every [[Communes of Balisca|commune]].

Cannabis has a long history in Balisca, possibly the longest in the [[Lurando-Abyala|New World]], as hemp production for fiber was carried as early as the 1540s. Similar attempts were made in other Mesogean colonies in [[Potocsí]], [[Asikyira]], and [[Balboa]], but only in Balisca did the crop also find success. The [[Maroon Confederacy]] was the first entity in what is now Balisca to explicitly legalize cannabis consumption, doing so in 1878.

In the 1940s, cannabis was used extensively by Baliscan service members in the [[Great Adonian War]]. The expanding use of cannabis outside of [[Araucaria]] in the 1950-1970s was associated with its popularization by returning servicemen, the [[Desconexión|''deesconexión'']] movement and later by [[W:Hippie|hippies]] that arrived in Balisca during the [[Great Migration]]. A confederal movement calling for [[W:Drug liberalization|recreational drug liberalization]] culminated in the 1962 [[Cannabis Initiative]], in which Balisca the first country in the world to formally legalize the cultivation, possession, acquisition and consumption of cannabis and its [[w:Cannabis (drug)#Preparations|by-products]]. By the early 1970s, a [[Secretariat of Education and Integration (Balisca)|Secretariat of Education]] report stated that an estimated 80% of Balisca high school students had tried cannabis at least once.

Balisca is the single-largest legal recreational cannabis market in the world, recording a total market worth of S/72.5 billion ({{I$|58 billion|link=yes}} billion) in 2020. Additionally, Balisca ranks first in the world in annual prevalence of cannabis use (with a 63% prevalence) amongst those polled.

